      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Throttle accelerates the physical overhead trolley; brake controls momentum
    and steering shifts the real suspended load. ACTION releases its cable. Sprint
    rewards an upright settled delivery and speed. Precision judges the final landing
    offset, tilt, preserved cargo, actual impacts and accumulated swing; rushing
    adds no precision bonus. Suspended Slalom requires the entire trailer to clear
    all four alternating marked openings in order before a successful platform landing
    can score. High-Wind Hauling applies real extra gusts and rewards successful
    forward transport through them, with impact and landing penalties. Release timing,
    swing and momentum matter; an early release or missed slalom opening is a failed
    slalom attempt.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
